    "description": "Job Category: Quality Control / Coffee Production Employment Type: Full-Time Work Place: Addis Ababa, Ethiopia (with travel to surrounding and coffee-producing regions required) Salary: based on the company scale Number of Vacancies: 1 Job Summary KANYA Coffee Export is seeking a skilled and detailed-oriented coffee cupper and quality supervisor. The successful candidate will lead Sensory evaluation, oversee quality control across the supply chain, and ensure that all coffee meets both company standards and international buyer requirements. The role involves close coordination with washing stations, the export processing mill, and maintains consistent quality form to export. Key Duties and Responsibilities Lead professional cupping session and final quality decisions for all commercial and specialty lots. Grade, classify, and approve coffee according to Ethiopia standards and specific buyer profiles. Supervise quality control activities at the company’s export processing mill (cleaning, hulling, grading, sorting, and preparation for export). Conduct regular quality audits at washing stations and draining facilities, identifying process gaps and driving corrective actions. Mange the preparation, evaluation, and export samples to international buyers. Maintain accurate quality records, cupping profiles, and inventory tracking of green stock. Prepare clear quality reports and present findings and recommendations to management. Work closely with suppliers and station managers to ensure consistent quality and continuous improvement. Perform other quality and export – related duties assigned by management.",
